{
  "id": "i-adjectives",
  "title": "い-Adjectives",
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "content": "**い-adjectives** end in い and conjugate directly : the い changes to signal tense and polarity. They can modify nouns directly and stand as predicates without any additional linking word."
    },
    {
      "type": "conjugation_table",
      "label": "高い (takai) : tall / expensive",
      "rows": [
        {
          "form": "present",
          "japanese": "高いです",
          "romaji": "takai desu",
          "english": "is tall"
        },
        {
          "form": "negative",
          "japanese": "高くないです",
          "romaji": "takakunai desu",
          "english": "is not tall"
        },
        {
          "form": "past",
          "japanese": "高かったです",
          "romaji": "takakatta desu",
          "english": "was tall"
        },
        {
          "form": "past negative",
          "japanese": "高くなかったです",
          "romaji": "takakunakatta desu",
          "english": "was not tall"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "example_table",
      "columns": [
        "japanese",
        "romaji",
        "english"
      ],
      "rows": [
        {
          "japanese": "この本は面白いです。",
          "romaji": "Kono hon wa omoshiroi desu.",
          "english": "This book is interesting."
        },
        {
          "japanese": "今日は寒くないです。",
          "romaji": "Kyō wa samukunai desu.",
          "english": "It's not cold today."
        },
        {
          "japanese": "子どもの頃、背が高かったです。",
          "romaji": "Kodomo no koro, se ga takakatta desu.",
          "english": "I was tall as a child."
        },
        {
          "japanese": "昨日の映画は長くなかったです。",
          "romaji": "Kinō no eiga wa nagakunakatta desu.",
          "english": "Yesterday's movie wasn't long."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "note",
      "content": "いい (good) is irregular. Its negative is よくない (not いくない) and its past is よかった (not いかった). This is the single most common い-adjective error for beginners."
    }
  ]
}